1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:01,367
<i>No more beating around the bush.</i>

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:02,400
<i> Straight to it!</i>

3
00:00:02,533 --> 00:00:05,000
<i> Where is Major Aglipay?</i>

4
00:00:05,133 --> 00:00:07,067
<i> Everyone who goes against us</i>

5
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:08,233
<i> ends up the same way.</i>

6
00:00:08,367 --> 00:00:09,800
<i>We still have
a lot of loose ends.</i>

7
00:00:09,933 --> 00:00:11,900
<i>That's why we have to control
the narrative.</i>

8
00:00:12,033 --> 00:00:14,900
<i>About Diego,
about how he betrayed you,</i>

9
00:00:15,033 --> 00:00:16,300
<i> I know everything.</i>

10
00:00:16,433 --> 00:00:18,467
<i>That's why he asked
for my forgiveness.</i>

11
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:20,167
<i>I will support you in your case.</i>

12
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:22,267
<i>Once I'm free, I'll make it up
to all of you.</i>

13
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:23,867
<i> Sources say he wasn't alone</i>

14
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,367
<i> in this drug operation.</i>

15
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:26,767
<i> Names have surfaced,</i>

16
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:28,333
<i> Major Miguel Delgado</i>

17
00:00:28,467 --> 00:00:29,733
<i>of the Bolagos
Provincial Police.</i>

18
00:00:29,867 --> 00:00:31,600
<i>I'm sure, someone's
manipulating this.</i>

19
00:00:31,733 --> 00:00:33,400
<i> They're trying to pin me down.</i>

20
00:00:33,533 --> 00:00:35,167
<i>You think we'd be scared of you</i>

21
00:00:35,333 --> 00:00:37,133
<i>just because you're a part
of a syndicate?</i>

22
00:00:37,267 --> 00:00:38,200
<i>I'm not a member
of a syndicate.</i>

23
00:00:38,333 --> 00:00:39,333
<i> Remember...</i>

24
00:00:39,467 --> 00:00:41,167
<i> you killed your batchmate!</i>

25
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:42,900
<i> You'll rot right here!</i>

26
00:00:43,033 --> 00:00:44,833
<i>I know someone who can help us.</i>

27
00:00:44,967 --> 00:00:46,467
<i> We just need to find her.</i>

28
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:47,600
<i> You again?</i>

29
00:00:47,733 --> 00:00:48,900
<i> What are you doing here?</i>

30
00:00:49,033 --> 00:00:50,400
<i> We're going to find Golda.</i>

31
00:00:50,533 --> 00:00:51,800
<i> I talked to a woman.</i>

32
00:00:51,933 --> 00:00:52,767
<i> She's really tight-lipped.</i>

33
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:54,300
<i>You just don't have a strategy.</i>

34
00:00:54,433 --> 00:00:55,000
<i> Let me try.</i>

35
00:00:55,133 --> 00:00:56,233
<i> I'm looking for Golda.</i>

36
00:00:56,367 --> 00:00:57,533
<i> She doesn't work here anymore,</i>

37
00:00:57,667 --> 00:00:59,233
<i> but we're cousins.</i>

38
00:00:59,367 --> 00:01:00,400
<i> Are you ready for your facial?</i>

39
00:01:00,533 --> 00:01:02,533
<i>- Shall we?
- He got in.</i>

40
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:32,467
Why?

41
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:35,000
That Korean took forever.

42
00:01:36,633 --> 00:01:38,700
You were just looking for
something wrong with him.

43
00:01:38,833 --> 00:01:40,700
Why didn't you
just give him time?

44
00:01:40,867 --> 00:01:43,400
He definitely
has a good strategy.

45
00:01:43,533 --> 00:01:45,100
Wow.

46
00:01:46,767 --> 00:01:48,467
Wait, why do you look like
you're flustered?

47
00:01:51,767 --> 00:01:53,667
I'm not flustered.

48
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:56,033
Of course, I'm just happy

49
00:01:56,167 --> 00:01:57,567
because unlike you,

50
00:01:57,700 --> 00:01:59,867
I'm sure he'll get useful
information.

51
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,433
Wow.

52
00:02:15,967 --> 00:02:16,967
Clarissa?

53
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:18,967
Ma'am...

54
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:20,167
Are you okay?

55
00:02:22,633 --> 00:02:24,033
It's nothing.

56
00:02:24,167 --> 00:02:25,300
I'm fine.

57
00:02:25,433 --> 00:02:27,267
Just a small matter.

58
00:02:29,533 --> 00:02:31,333
You look sad.

59
00:02:31,467 --> 00:02:33,933
I noticed it this morning.

60
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:37,100
And now, you're tearing up.

61
00:02:38,633 --> 00:02:40,433
Is there something wrong?

62
00:02:42,233 --> 00:02:44,167
No, Ma'am...

63
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:46,033
I'm sorry.

64
00:02:47,533 --> 00:02:51,500
I shouldn't have brought
my problems here to work.

65
00:02:51,633 --> 00:02:53,733
How can we care for others

66
00:02:53,867 --> 00:02:56,500
if we ourselves,
at the foundation,

67
00:02:56,633 --> 00:02:59,433
can't take care of each other?

68
00:02:59,567 --> 00:03:00,900
I've been stressed

69
00:03:01,033 --> 00:03:04,833
about everything that's
happening to my family.

70
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:08,167
There's also something
I didn't tell you

71
00:03:08,300 --> 00:03:09,700
because I was embarrassed.

72
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:14,633
My husband is in jail,

73
00:03:14,767 --> 00:03:18,033
but he didn't do anything wrong.

74
00:03:19,033 --> 00:03:21,267
It was all a setup.

75
00:03:24,733 --> 00:03:26,367
But...

76
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:29,600
But the hard part is...

77
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:31,533
His best friend,

78
00:03:31,667 --> 00:03:34,233
the one I considered
a true friend,

79
00:03:34,367 --> 00:03:36,867
betrayed us.

80
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:41,767
So now, I don't know
who to trust.

81
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:44,233
I thought I could handle it.

82
00:03:45,700 --> 00:03:48,567
Turns out, I couldn't.

83
00:03:49,367 --> 00:03:53,767
I'm terrified for myself
and for my family.

84
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:56,833
I didn't know you were going
through that.

85
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:00,467
You know, you don't have
to go through it alone.

86
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:05,000
You know, my husband
is kind of well-connected.

87
00:04:05,133 --> 00:04:06,300
Maybe you'd like me to ask him
to take a look

88
00:04:06,433 --> 00:04:07,900
at your husband's case.

89
00:04:12,967 --> 00:04:14,333
But, Joey...

90
00:04:14,467 --> 00:04:16,500
I also noticed that...

91
00:04:16,633 --> 00:04:19,067
you're really impressed
with that guy.

92
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:21,667
Is it because
he's handsome, tall,

93
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:23,733
cool, and skilled in fighting?

94
00:04:23,867 --> 00:04:26,633
You know what, don't bother,

95
00:04:26,767 --> 00:04:28,467
because all of the above.

96
00:04:30,367 --> 00:04:33,133
And you know what I really like
about him?

97
00:04:33,867 --> 00:04:36,200
He's honest with me.

98
00:04:36,333 --> 00:04:39,100
Do you know? He wasn't afraid
to tell me the truth

99
00:04:39,233 --> 00:04:41,700
about what could happen
to Godfather Diego.

100
00:04:42,867 --> 00:04:43,767
Not only that,

101
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:46,600
he didn't treat me like a child.

102
00:04:46,733 --> 00:04:47,733
He didn't sugarcoat things

103
00:04:47,867 --> 00:04:51,400
to make it seem okay
when it wasn't.

104
00:04:51,533 --> 00:04:55,333
Because he believes I can face
any problem, no matter what.

105
00:05:06,167 --> 00:05:07,800
It's fine.

106
00:05:10,933 --> 00:05:12,333
Never mind.

107
00:05:14,867 --> 00:05:16,700
Are you sure, Clarissa?

108
00:05:18,633 --> 00:05:20,033
Yes, Ma'am...

109
00:05:20,167 --> 00:05:22,533
Just listening to me...

110
00:05:23,333 --> 00:05:25,400
is already a huge thing.

111
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:29,533
Ma'am, I'll go back
to work now.

112
00:05:29,667 --> 00:05:31,267
Okay.

113
00:05:45,933 --> 00:05:47,467
He's here.

114
00:05:51,033 --> 00:05:52,167
So?

115
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:56,100
So, guys, the service
was so good.

116
00:05:56,233 --> 00:06:00,533
Their facial is so relaxing.

117
00:06:00,667 --> 00:06:01,433
And I literally slept.

118
00:06:01,567 --> 00:06:03,500
I even snored.

119
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,800
Good for you, I guess.

120
00:06:08,967 --> 00:06:11,533
We don't care
about your spa review.

121
00:06:11,667 --> 00:06:15,067
What we want to know
is about Golda.

122
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:16,633
Okay, okay.

123
00:06:16,767 --> 00:06:19,267
So here's what I found out.

124
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:22,833
The receptionist is her cousin.

125
00:06:23,567 --> 00:06:27,133
Then Golda handed over
the spa management to her,

126
00:06:27,267 --> 00:06:30,300
but technically,
Golda is still the owner.

127
00:06:30,433 --> 00:06:33,167
She had to leave, indefinitely.

128
00:06:34,167 --> 00:06:36,433
You were gone for so long,
that's all you found out?

129
00:06:37,367 --> 00:06:39,467
So she's still in hiding.

130
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:42,167
But do they still contact
each other?

131
00:06:42,333 --> 00:06:43,900
Good question, Peter.

132
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:47,033
Yes, they still talk.

133
00:06:47,167 --> 00:06:49,167
Did she give it to you,

134
00:06:49,300 --> 00:06:50,400
Golda's number?

135
00:06:50,533 --> 00:06:51,833
No.

136
00:06:51,967 --> 00:06:53,200
What?

137
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:55,500
I can't just ask for it.

138
00:06:55,633 --> 00:06:57,400
It'll be too obvious.

139
00:06:59,533 --> 00:07:03,000
So you didn't get anything?

140
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:07,667
Don't worry.

141
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:09,000
I know what to do.

142
00:07:09,133 --> 00:07:11,033
Yes, yes, I'm sure.

143
00:07:11,167 --> 00:07:12,733
Sure...

144
00:07:22,833 --> 00:07:24,500
There she is.

145
00:07:37,467 --> 00:07:39,300
Okay, let's go.

146
00:08:11,967 --> 00:08:13,300
So...

147
00:08:13,433 --> 00:08:15,600
If Golda used to be
a distributor,

148
00:08:15,733 --> 00:08:17,033
according to your father,
Joey...

149
00:08:18,167 --> 00:08:19,867
she might know people
in the syndicate,

150
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:22,600
like Theresa Park.

151
00:08:22,767 --> 00:08:24,433
It's possible.

152
00:08:24,567 --> 00:08:25,967
And if that's the case,

153
00:08:26,100 --> 00:08:28,167
we'll be hitting two birds
with one stone.

154
00:08:28,300 --> 00:08:31,033
She can help dad

155
00:08:31,167 --> 00:08:33,067
and she can help you find
Theresa Park.

156
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:34,733
Yes.

157
00:08:40,367 --> 00:08:41,700
Wait, the bag's gone.

158
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:44,267
She left it inside.

159
00:08:56,567 --> 00:08:58,233
What's our next move?

160
00:08:58,367 --> 00:09:00,367
If my instinct is correct...

161
00:09:01,300 --> 00:09:02,700
that bag contains money,

162
00:09:02,833 --> 00:09:04,667
and Golda will come to get it.

163
00:09:04,800 --> 00:09:05,733
That's how she collects.

164
00:09:05,867 --> 00:09:08,000
No paper trail.

165
00:09:08,133 --> 00:09:10,333
Oh, you're good.

166
00:09:11,467 --> 00:09:12,533
Yes, sure.

167
00:09:12,667 --> 00:09:15,133
I'm an agent for a reason.

168
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:20,233
Wait, so that means...

169
00:09:20,367 --> 00:09:22,200
Golda is coming from there,
right?

170
00:09:22,333 --> 00:09:24,200
But when? When?

171
00:09:24,333 --> 00:09:26,533
Well, we don't know yet.

172
00:09:26,667 --> 00:09:28,300
But she will show up.

173
00:09:28,467 --> 00:09:30,467
You don't know? So what?
Do we just wait for her

174
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:32,333
to arrive here?

175
00:09:34,933 --> 00:09:35,967
Trust me.

176
00:09:56,033 --> 00:09:57,600
I'm getting sleepy.

177
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:01,100
I still have
a livestream tomorrow.

178
00:10:01,267 --> 00:10:02,600
You know what?

179
00:10:02,733 --> 00:10:05,200
Just keep me updated.

180
00:10:05,333 --> 00:10:06,567
Wow.

181
00:10:06,700 --> 00:10:07,867
You're leaving us?

182
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,467
Livestream?

183
00:10:10,433 --> 00:10:11,867
I can wait here alone.

184
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:13,600
No, Jin Ho.

185
00:10:13,733 --> 00:10:14,700
I'll stay with you.

186
00:10:16,900 --> 00:10:19,467
I'll stay with you also.

187
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:21,467
I'm not leaving as long
as Joey's here.

188
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:23,400
I'll stay.

189
00:10:23,533 --> 00:10:24,500
I'll stay.

190
00:10:24,633 --> 00:10:27,633
We really shouldn't leave
Jin Ho alone.

191
00:10:27,767 --> 00:10:30,367
He's done so much for us.

192
00:10:31,700 --> 00:10:33,833
Well, I've done a lot too.

193
00:10:34,867 --> 00:10:35,933
I don't know about you, guys.

194
00:10:36,067 --> 00:10:37,767
But I'm leaving, okay?

195
00:10:37,900 --> 00:10:39,433
I still have a livestream
tomorrow.

196
00:10:39,567 --> 00:10:41,033
Bye.

197
00:11:00,967 --> 00:11:02,600
There she is.

198
00:11:10,967 --> 00:11:12,500
It's Golda.

199
00:11:50,067 --> 00:11:52,067
Joey, Joey, wait, wait,
wait, wait.

200
00:11:52,200 --> 00:11:53,300
Where are you going?

201
00:11:53,433 --> 00:11:54,800
- Stay here.
- I'm going to talk to Golda.

202
00:11:54,933 --> 00:11:56,833
No. She might just get scared
of you.

203
00:11:57,933 --> 00:12:00,200
Why would she be scared of me?

204
00:12:00,333 --> 00:12:02,967
I'm such a sweetheart.

205
00:12:03,100 --> 00:12:07,200
I just want to confront her
about lying about my dad.

206
00:12:28,467 --> 00:12:29,933
Maybe I can talk to her

207
00:12:30,067 --> 00:12:31,833
like I did with her cousin.

208
00:12:34,433 --> 00:12:38,233
Can you stop
with your oppa charm?

209
00:12:38,367 --> 00:12:39,933
I can do this.

210
00:12:40,067 --> 00:12:41,667
I got this, okay?

211
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:42,967
I was able to do it before.

212
00:12:43,100 --> 00:12:44,600
I can do it again.

213
00:12:44,733 --> 00:12:48,600
So you guys stay here,
especially you.

214
00:12:48,767 --> 00:12:50,333
You stay here.

215
00:12:50,467 --> 00:12:51,967
Don't be stubborn.

216
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:14,233
Don't worry, Peter.

217
00:13:15,067 --> 00:13:18,867
Your time will come
to charm a girl too.

218
00:13:57,733 --> 00:13:59,400
How did you find me?

219
00:13:59,533 --> 00:14:01,167
Relax.

220
00:14:01,300 --> 00:14:03,867
No one knows you're here.

221
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:06,667
If you managed to track me down,

222
00:14:06,800 --> 00:14:08,433
then probably so did they.

223
00:14:10,800 --> 00:14:12,567
They?

224
00:14:12,700 --> 00:14:14,567
Who are they?

225
00:14:15,700 --> 00:14:17,767
Who are you afraid of, Golda?

226
00:14:17,900 --> 00:14:19,967
Is this the same person
who ordered you to lie

227
00:14:20,100 --> 00:14:21,533
about Major Delgado?

228
00:14:40,033 --> 00:14:40,867
Hey!

229
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,900
Boss Trigger,
you finally came back!

230
00:14:43,933 --> 00:14:46,500
Of course, I missed you, guys!

231
00:14:46,633 --> 00:14:47,900
Welcome back, Boss!

232
00:14:48,033 --> 00:14:49,167
What's up?

233
00:14:49,300 --> 00:14:51,967
Are we partying now?

234
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:53,467
Guys, Trigger's here!

235
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:55,433
Let's get our party started!

236
00:14:55,567 --> 00:14:57,567
Yes, let's get it started!

237
00:14:57,700 --> 00:15:02,600
- Trigger! Trigger!
- Trigger! Trigger!

238
00:15:19,533 --> 00:15:22,133
Trigger, this is for you.

239
00:15:22,267 --> 00:15:23,967
- From my wife.
- Hey!

240
00:15:24,100 --> 00:15:26,133
Banana, it's sweet.

241
00:15:31,733 --> 00:15:33,567
It's taking too long!

242
00:15:33,700 --> 00:15:34,733
- Joey!
- Joey!

243
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:36,300
No...

244
00:15:37,333 --> 00:15:38,800
Joey!

245
00:15:42,367 --> 00:15:44,067
I'm not lying.

246
00:15:44,200 --> 00:15:45,767
Everything I told you is true.

247
00:15:45,900 --> 00:15:47,600
So can you just stop chasing me?

248
00:15:47,733 --> 00:15:49,233
Goodbye!

249
00:15:49,367 --> 00:15:52,067
Golda, but you're guilty.

250
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:53,733
I can see it.

251
00:15:53,867 --> 00:15:55,267
Because I know Major Delgado.

252
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:56,900
He's a good man.

253
00:15:57,033 --> 00:15:58,267
So I know you feel guilty

254
00:15:58,400 --> 00:16:00,567
for everything you did to him.

255
00:16:03,333 --> 00:16:04,567
Golda.

256
00:16:04,700 --> 00:16:06,000
What?

257
00:16:07,167 --> 00:16:08,167
Who are you?

258
00:16:08,333 --> 00:16:10,167
Didn't I say I'd handle this?

259
00:16:11,400 --> 00:16:12,900
I'm Miguel Delgado's child.

260
00:16:14,167 --> 00:16:16,433
Do you know you ruined
our family?

261
00:16:16,567 --> 00:16:17,633
My father went to jail,

262
00:16:17,767 --> 00:16:20,033
and my parents almost separated
because of you!

263
00:16:20,167 --> 00:16:21,633
Because of your lies!

264
00:16:21,767 --> 00:16:23,133
So if you still have
a conscience,

265
00:16:23,267 --> 00:16:26,000
can you take back what you said
and tell the truth?

266
00:16:26,133 --> 00:16:28,467
You know what happened
to Parak, right?

267
00:16:29,533 --> 00:16:31,467
To Major Aglipay?

268
00:16:32,467 --> 00:16:34,633
I don't to end up like him!

269
00:16:35,733 --> 00:16:37,867
So just tell Miguel
that I'm sorry.

270
00:16:38,500 --> 00:16:40,100
He'll understand me too.

271
00:16:41,300 --> 00:16:42,267
Golda, please.

272
00:16:43,367 --> 00:16:44,733
Don't come near!

273
00:16:44,867 --> 00:16:46,233
Stop!

274
00:16:48,533 --> 00:16:50,000
Don't come near, okay?

275
00:16:50,133 --> 00:16:51,633
Golda...

276
00:16:51,767 --> 00:16:53,533
please listen to us first.

277
00:16:55,867 --> 00:16:57,133
Please.

278
00:16:57,267 --> 00:16:59,067
Stop chasing me, okay?

279
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:01,067
Don't follow!

280
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:03,667
I know you can't shoot, Golda.

281
00:17:04,667 --> 00:17:06,733
Golda, please!
Have mercy on my father!

282
00:17:08,933 --> 00:17:10,900
Don't follow me!

283
00:17:18,933 --> 00:17:20,933
She can't escape!

284
00:17:30,367 --> 00:17:31,333
Oppa!

285
00:17:31,467 --> 00:17:32,667
Oppa, oppa, this way!
Oppa, this way!

286
00:17:32,800 --> 00:17:34,067
Go!

287
00:17:46,367 --> 00:17:47,700
Golda!

288
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:12,867
- Golda!
- Golda!

289
00:18:27,433 --> 00:18:29,133
That's ours.

290
00:18:29,267 --> 00:18:31,300
Go! Grab some!

291
00:18:32,967 --> 00:18:33,900
Thank you!

292
00:18:34,033 --> 00:18:34,800
Let's just share.

293
00:18:34,933 --> 00:18:35,867
Okay.

294
00:18:36,933 --> 00:18:37,967
Bro!

295
00:18:38,100 --> 00:18:40,733
Is there something wrong
with your eyes?

296
00:18:40,867 --> 00:18:43,600
You've been staring at me
ever since I sat down.

297
00:18:43,733 --> 00:18:44,800
Who are you?

298
00:18:44,933 --> 00:18:46,833
Who's this? Is he gay?

299
00:18:46,967 --> 00:18:48,167
You stare so intensely.

300
00:18:48,300 --> 00:18:50,833
That used to be a cop, Boss!

301
00:18:50,967 --> 00:18:54,300
A terror of drug busts,
but actually a cop killer.

302
00:18:54,433 --> 00:18:55,433
Right?

303
00:18:57,767 --> 00:18:59,133
Killer...

304
00:18:59,267 --> 00:19:01,800
Terror of drug busts...

305
00:19:03,500 --> 00:19:07,067
Ramon Orbos,
the cop they said I killed...

306
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:09,633
do you know him?

307
00:19:12,867 --> 00:19:15,467
Do you know my mom's favorite
thing to say to me?

308
00:19:16,833 --> 00:19:19,567
Don't talk to strangers.

309
00:19:23,733 --> 00:19:25,067
Eat!

310
00:19:39,233 --> 00:19:42,200
It's going to be harder
to find Golda now!

311
00:19:42,333 --> 00:19:44,167
You think?

312
00:19:44,300 --> 00:19:45,367
Yes!

313
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:48,567
Because she knows
we're after her now.

314
00:19:48,700 --> 00:19:50,467
How did she escape?

315
00:19:50,600 --> 00:19:51,367
Of course, she got scared.

316
00:19:51,500 --> 00:19:53,800
She saw we were going
to corner her.

317
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:57,333
Well, that's because
you showed up.

318
00:19:57,467 --> 00:20:00,233
Joey, our conversation
was going smoothly.

319
00:20:00,367 --> 00:20:02,767
I charmed her, I got it done.

320
00:20:02,933 --> 00:20:04,567
But you, you were so stubborn.

321
00:20:04,700 --> 00:20:05,967
You didn't listen.

322
00:20:06,100 --> 00:20:08,300
You were told not to go near,
and you still rushed in.

323
00:20:08,433 --> 00:20:09,833
Look at what happened now.

324
00:20:10,833 --> 00:20:12,433
She escaped.

325
00:20:12,567 --> 00:20:15,200
Right? And we almost got shot.

326
00:20:15,333 --> 00:20:16,633
You took forever!

327
00:20:16,767 --> 00:20:18,000
And what did you want me to do?

328
00:20:18,133 --> 00:20:20,700
The woman we're after is right
in front of me now.

329
00:20:20,833 --> 00:20:21,533
And I do nothing?

330
00:20:21,667 --> 00:20:22,967
We all know that.

331
00:20:23,100 --> 00:20:24,067
You're not using your brain.

332
00:20:24,200 --> 00:20:25,800
Sorry, okay?
I'm not a robot like you.

333
00:20:25,933 --> 00:20:26,967
Wait, wait.

334
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:27,867
Why are you picking
a fight with Joey?

335
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:29,500
Are you fighting Joey?

336
00:20:31,400 --> 00:20:32,800
Guys...

337
00:20:32,933 --> 00:20:33,933
Let's go home.

338
00:20:35,067 --> 00:20:37,467
Get some rest.
We need to take some rest.

339
00:20:37,600 --> 00:20:39,933
Let's go.

340
00:20:40,067 --> 00:20:41,700
You guys go ahead.

341
00:20:41,833 --> 00:20:43,500
Aren't you coming?

342
00:20:43,633 --> 00:20:45,667
I said go ahead without me,
right?

343
00:20:46,867 --> 00:20:48,700
All right, be careful.

344
00:20:53,467 --> 00:20:54,833
Go.

345
00:21:11,967 --> 00:21:13,467
I think my work here
is done.

346
00:21:13,600 --> 00:21:14,400
On her shoulder.

347
00:21:14,533 --> 00:21:15,833
It will lead us to Golda.

348
00:21:15,967 --> 00:21:17,100
We have to find her.

349
00:21:17,233 --> 00:21:18,533
You're going out?

350
00:21:18,667 --> 00:21:19,833
We are going out.

351
00:21:19,967 --> 00:21:20,967
I'm coming with you.

352
00:21:21,100 --> 00:21:22,333
We can still check on Golda.

353
00:21:22,467 --> 00:21:23,400
Let's go.

354
00:21:23,533 --> 00:21:26,167
Looks like he wants
to sabotage all our work.

355
00:21:26,300 --> 00:21:29,200
He'll use anyone
to get close to you.

356
00:21:29,333 --> 00:21:31,067
He really won't leave me alone.

357
00:21:31,200 --> 00:21:32,533
He's ruthless.

358
00:21:32,667 --> 00:21:33,600
The syndicate is here.

359
00:21:33,733 --> 00:21:34,900
They're about to enter the spa.

360
00:21:35,033 --> 00:21:36,667
- What?
- Where's Golda?

361
00:21:36,800 --> 00:21:37,800
We have to go!

362
00:21:37,933 --> 00:21:40,133
On the count of three,
you run, okay?

363
00:21:40,267 --> 00:21:42,233
I'll cover you.

364
00:21:42,400 --> 00:21:45,300
One, two, three! You run!

365
00:21:45,433 --> 00:21:46,500
There they are!

366
00:21:46,633 --> 00:21:47,767
Go! Go!

367
00:21:47,900 --> 00:21:49,233
Jin Ho, let's go!
